# Documentation and Standards Rules

## 1. General Rules
- All generated content must be in French
- Use autocomplete and supercomplete for documentation and code
- Course structure: 5 days (6.5 hours per day)
- Distribution: 30-40% theory, 60-70% practice

## 2. Documentation Structure
### 2.1 Section Order (mandatory)
1. Introduction et installation de Windows Server
2. DNS
3. Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
4. Utilisateurs et ordinateurs Active Directory
5. Unités d'organisation (OU)
6. Strategies de groupes (GPO)
7. Gestion AD DS en PowerShell

### 2.2 Exercise Format
```markdown
## Exercise X.Y - Title
Description and context

<details>
<summary>Solution X.Y</summary>
Detailed solution
</details>
```
- Never add exercises without asking first

## 3. Diagram Standards
### 3.1 Format and Storage
- Format: exclusively .drawio
- Storage: "diagrams" folder
- Base: use structure_reseau_geographic.drawio as template
- Never generate images (conversion script will be used)
- Use standard XML structure for .drawio files
- Use < and > characters directly (no HTML entities)

### 3.2 Style Specifications
- Color codes:
  * Network services/DNS: light blue (#dae8fc)
  * AD DS/Controllers: light gray (#f5f5f5)
  * OU/Structure: light orange (#ffe6cc)
  * Actions/Flow: light yellow (#fff2cc)
- Connections and Arrows: curved, light gray with 65% opacity
- Containers: sized to fit text
- File naming: snake_case in French

## 4. Virtual Infrastructure
### 4.1 Hardware Configuration
- 32GB RAM per student machine
- Windows Server 2022 installed

### 4.2 Virtual Machines
- 1 main server (future DC)
- 1 client workstation
- Optional: 1 additional server (second DC)


## 5. PowerShell Standards
### 5.1 Usage
- Include basic commands
- Learning through immersion
- Context-relevant commands only

### 5.2 Documentation Format
- Introduce with "En PowerShell:"
- Use ```powershell code blocks
- Commands must be concise and commented in French



## 6. Naming Standards

### For GPOs:

GPO-[Type]-[Name]

- Types: Securite, Configuration, Restrictions
- Standard parameters:
  * Password length: always use "Password1!" as a password

### For Groups:

[Type]-[Groupe Scope]-[Name]

- **Type**: **S-** for Security or **D-** for Distribution. All uppercase.
- **Group Scope**: **DL-** for Domain Local, **G-** for Global, **U-** for Universal. All uppercase.
- Only first letter uppercase for each word of Name



## 7. DNS Infrastructure
- Root domain: computerelectronics.be
- **Important**: The domain structure is in diagrams/structure_reseau_geographic_zones.drawio

## 8. Exercise Creation Rules
- Always ask permission before adding new exercises
- Wait for explicit user confirmation
- Exercises must follow immediately after their theoretical section
- Include practical examples based on computerelectronics.be

## 9. IP Addressing Standards

- IP addressing schemes to align with the new standard (192.168.0.x), both in the documentation and in the diagrams
- The ip adresses must be in a way that can indeed be implemented during the course with the virtual machines
  
## 10. Documentation mood

- Use a friendly and approachable tone
- Use simple and easy-to-understand language
- Use short sentences and paragraphs
- Use active voice. The course is interactive and you will be asked to do things
- Use the second person (you) when you are asked to do things
- Don't use the first person (I) when you are doing things
- Use the present tense
- Use the future tense when you are asking for things to be done
- Exercises are done by the student (Ex: "Vous allez créer un serveur")
- Examples are doing by the instructor and the students at the same time (Ex: "Nous allons créer un serveur")
- When creating instructions, use bold to highlight the most important elements of the phrase. The idea is that the student can read really fast and understand what is important.

